       layout (this component shares a row with the headline column
       there, leaving real room beside it) — but stacked full-width at
       this size, that gutter doesn't exist, and the same negative left
       offset that placed it there instead pushed it off the left edge
       of the viewport, clipped rather than scrollable (see .dy-hero's
       own overflow:hidden). Pulled back to the artwork's own edge
       instead, the same accommodation .dy-hero__ais-ask already makes
       just above for the identical reason. */
    .dy-hero__ais-label--memory {
      left: 0%;
    }
